                    briefing_text_r2:       `Redesign the journey under the <strong>€2.0M cap</strong> and the <strong>30% margin floor</strong>. The obvious move — add three features, hire 60 coaches, automate everything — is exactly the trap: more surface area for co-destruction, and the cap blown. The discipline is <em>subtraction</em> and smarter integration: a <strong>light-touch onboarding wizard</strong> (80% of the data, 20% of the friction), an honest “comfort vs savings” reset, usage-driven coaching, and maybe a curated peer community. Each option costs money and trades off churn, satisfaction and margin.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Set the co-creation rule & contain the misuse`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Author the <strong>co-creation rule</strong>: what the firm provides, what the customer must contribute, and what happens when either side fails — and make the customer's part <em>easy</em>, not a barrier. Simultaneously, a ~4,000-strong cluster is gaming the savings guarantee for €22 credits (<strong>€88,000 and rising</strong>). You can enforce (claw back, tighten terms for all 240,000 — fast but trust-eroding), <strong>design it out</strong> (cap triggers, detect anomalies, reframe around verified behaviour), or convert the gamers. Weigh €88k against the signal you send the <em>236,000 loyal customers</em>.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Pre-empt the next cold snap`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Present a 60-day plan to the board. The recovery test bites: <strong>the onboarding wizard cut drop-off only half as much as hoped</strong>, and a <strong>second cold snap arrives in 45 days</strong>. Sequence the plan so the households still mid-onboarding are re-engaged before the cold hits, ease the friction <em>without re-opening the co-destruction gap</em>, and defend redesign to a board where the CMO wants a discount and the CFO wants the guarantee scrapped. A second wave of backlash before the fix lands makes the press narrative permanent.`,

                    r1_worst_label:         `Which two touchpoints concentrate the co-destruction? Pick the primary failure point.`,
                    r1_whose_label:         `At your worst touchpoint, whose resources failed (Plé's co-destruction lens)?`,
                    r1_diagnosis_label:     `How candidly does your team frame churn as an interaction problem, not a marketing/pricing problem? (%)`,
                    r1_diagnosis_readout:   `Treating churn as interaction design, not a discount:`,
